1
00:00:00,610 --> 00:00:03,870
(Amy:)I think we need
to face the cold, hard truth:

2
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:07,640
(Amy:)I was sexually aroused
by Penny's friend Zack.

3
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:09,310
(Sheldon:)Hang on. I don't know

4
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:11,520
(Sheldon:)that we've given
the alien parasite hypothesis

5
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:13,620
(Sheldon:)a fair shake.

6
00:00:13,620 --> 00:00:14,690
(Amy:)Let's look at this logically.

7
00:00:14,690 --> 00:00:16,620
I have a stomach; I get hungry.

8
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:19,720
I have genitals; I have the
potential for sexual arousal.

9
00:00:19,720 --> 00:00:22,690
(Sheldon:)A cross we all must bear.

10
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:27,800
(Sheldon:)You know, in difficult
moments like this,

11
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:30,800
(Sheldon:)I often turn to a force
greater than myself.

12
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,800
(Amy:)Religion?

13
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:33,000
Star Trek.

14
00:00:34,010 --> 00:00:36,410
Did you see
Star Trek: The Motion Picture?

15
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:38,440
(Leonard:)No.
Don't. It's terrible. However...

16
00:00:38,440 --> 00:00:40,940
(Sheldon:)in it, we learn that

17
00:00:40,950 --> 00:00:43,980
(Sheldon:)when Spock finds himself
drawn off the path of logic

18
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:47,850
(Sheldon:)by feelings bubbling up from his
human half, he suppresses them

19
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:50,620
(Sheldon:)using the Vulcan mental
discipline of Kolinar.

20
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:52,720
(Amy:)Are you suggesting
we live our lives

21
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:55,330
(Amy:)guided by the philosophies
found in cheap science fiction?

22
00:00:55,330 --> 00:01:01,020
"Cheap science fiction"?

